WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.051
A useful finding identifies the
requirement,

2
00:00:03.171 --> 00:00:05.752
the specific design evidence and the gap.

3
00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:09.776
For example: drawing revision B contains a
cleaning pocket

4
00:00:09.896 --> 00:00:13.544
that has no reviewed rationale against the
cleaning concept.

5
00:00:13.664 --> 00:00:17.504
Assign an owner and define what evidence
would support closure.

6
00:00:17.624 --> 00:00:22.296
Avoid replacing the finding with a vague
status such as vendor to confirm.

7
00:00:22.416 --> 00:00:24.976
A due date helps manage work, but it does

8
00:00:25.096 --> 00:00:27.763
not establish that the design is suitable.

9
00:00:28.383 --> 00:00:31.497
Our teaching review uses three distinct
outcomes:

10
00:00:31.617 --> 00:00:35.052
design evidence adequate, an open design
finding,

11
00:00:35.172 --> 00:00:37.327
or a proposed requirement change.

12
00:00:37.447 --> 00:00:41.713
These are course labels, not mandatory
regulatory terminology.

13
00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:44.186
If the vendor cannot meet a requirement,

14
00:00:44.306 --> 00:00:48.466
assess options with the appropriate
process and quality expertise.

15
00:00:48.586 --> 00:00:53.130
Do not close the gap by deleting the
requirement without impact review.

16
00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.344
A proposed change remains a proposal until

17
00:00:56.464 --> 00:00:59.152
the applicable approval process accepts
it.

18
00:00:59.772 --> 00:01:02.950
Conditional progression concerns a
particular next

19
00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:06.590
qualification activity, not unrestricted
production.

20
00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:09.612
In the fictional case, a missing product-
contact

21
00:01:09.732 --> 00:01:13.294
gasket basis prevents a final materials
conclusion.

22
00:01:13.414 --> 00:01:18.150
For example, a proposed transition to IQ
may be limited to equipment

23
00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.726
identification checks unaffected by the
gasket gap.

24
00:01:21.846 --> 00:01:24.790
This requires a documented assessment of
no

25
00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.726
significant impact on that next activity

26
00:01:27.846 --> 00:01:30.833
and authorization by responsible
personnel.

27
00:01:30.953 --> 00:01:33.406
Gasket-dependent checks remain on hold.

28
00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.596
Preparing documents alone is

29
00:01:35.716 --> 00:01:38.361
not progression to a qualification stage,

30
00:01:38.481 --> 00:01:41.553
and neither activity authorizes
manufacturing.

31
00:01:41.673 --> 00:01:45.812
The responsible personnel need a
documented impact assessment

32
00:01:45.932 --> 00:01:49.004
and an authorized decision for the
proposed stage.

33
00:01:49.124 --> 00:01:51.418
Do not assume that the training author,

34
00:01:51.538 --> 00:01:54.546
supplier or learner can grant a site’s
approval.

35
00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:59.176
When a gasket specification changes,
retain the earlier baseline

36
00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:02.027
and record why the new design was
selected.

37
00:02:02.147 --> 00:02:05.304
Revisit contact compatibility, cleaning
assumptions

38
00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:08.027
and verification plans as appropriate.

39
00:02:08.147 --> 00:02:11.539
Update affected conclusions through the
quality system.

40
00:02:11.659 --> 00:02:15.659
The record should allow another reviewer
to reconstruct the decision

41
00:02:15.779 --> 00:02:17.779
without relying on memory.

42
00:02:17.899 --> 00:02:20.694
Your activity is to write an action
closure

43
00:02:20.814 --> 00:02:23.075
that references the revised evidence

44
00:02:23.195 --> 00:02:25.734
and preserves any outstanding later tests.
